# Workspace-level ignores. Patterns apply across desktop/ and mobile/ so the
# same .gitignore is the single source of truth for both subprojects.

# ─── Secrets — nothing below this heading may ever reach a commit ───
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Android signing material. `*.keystore` alone does NOT cover `.jks`, which is
# the extension keytool actually produces by default — both are listed.
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/keystore.properties
!**/debug.keystore          # Android debug keystore is committed by convention

# Machine-local SDK paths and agent settings (leak the developer's drive layout)
**/local.properties
.claude/
**/.claude/

# ─── Personal configuration ───
# The shipped persona.md is the professional default. A local override is
# personal to whoever runs it and is never committed.
persona.local.md
**/persona.local.md

# ─── Node / npm ───
**/node_modules/
**/.npm/
**/.pnpm-store/

# ─── Electron build artifacts (desktop/) ───
**/out/
**/release/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/.cache/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright browser bundle (downloaded at install time, not source)
**/pw-browsers/

# ─── Android build artifacts (mobile/) ───
# Scoped to mobile/ on purpose. A blanket `**/build/` would also swallow
# desktop/build/ (icon.png + electron-builder inputs, which ARE source), and a
# `!desktop/build/` negation cannot rescue it — git never descends into an
# excluded directory, so nothing inside it can be re-included.
**/.gradle/
mobile/**/build/
**/captures/
**/*.iml
**/.idea/
**/.cxx/

# Avatar payload staged into the APK by avatar-bundler — generated, not source.
# See mobile/android/avatar-bundler/README.md.
mobile/android/app/src/main/assets/avatar/

# ─── Logs ───
*.log
**/*.log

# ─── OS / IDE noise ───
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
